    "md5": "6d1d393715c2220613f231a89a377e40",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1808,
    "chunk_text": "CDB organizes SMB Fair to empower local enterprises\n\nBuilding a strong building block to empower Small and Medium Businesses (SMB) in Sri Lanka, Citizens Development Business Finance PLC (CDB) organizes a landmark two-day event in Kandy built around a single and powerful promise: Experience The Best of Local Business, All in One Place.\n\nFollowing five SMB fairs in Colombo, scheduling the next in Kandy is a significant milestone in CDB\u2019s focus of empowering SMBs across the country.\u00a0 Scheduled for the 19th and 20th at Sahas Uyana, Kandy, this fair will bring together SMBs in a single location, all powered by CDB. By removing every financial barrier between local entrepreneurs and a premium event platform, CDB ensures this fair becomes a true celebration of Sri Lankan enterprise.\n\n\u201cThe theme \u201cExperience The Best of Local Business, All in One Place\u201d is not merely a tagline,\u201d states Assistant General Manager \u2013 Finance Chamath Siriwardana. \u201cIt is a declaration of intent, a statement that Sri Lanka\u2019s most vibrant local businesses deserve to be seen and supported, and that CDB is the institution committed to making that happen. As a leading corporate steward, CDB is happy to lead the charge in empowering SMBs as the engine of growth for this nation. Every aspect of the fair is designed to showcase the strength of local entrepreneurship, while highlighting CDB\u2019s role as a catalyst for growth.\u201d\n\nAt the heart of the event lies CDB\u2019s primary action: to create the definitive local business showcase of the year in Kandy. The merchant participants will have access to the patpat.lk platform, guaranteeing these SMBs the unique opportunity of expanding both reach and business growth. It\u2019s also a promise of zero cost to the businesses and maximum opportunity for exposure."
  },
