    "md5": "46fca696546309c3fd8bdc70c2832c71",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "Sysco LABS\u2019 Product Nexus explores future of AI-driven product innovation and discovery\n\nThe Panelists for Product Nexus (from left): Fawaz Haniffa \u2013 Lead Product Manager; Dilshan Weerabahu \u2013 Lead Product Manager; Amila Jayawickrama \u2013 Associate Manager \u2013 Business Analysis; Atheek Razick \u2013 Senior Lead \u2013 Business Analysis and Moderator: Vishmie Perera \u2013 Business Analyst.\n\nSysco LABS recently brought together professionals across Product Management and Business Analysis through \u201cProduct Nexus\u201d \u2014 a platform within its broader Nexus series designed to foster industry dialogue and knowledge sharing around emerging trends shaping the future of enterprise technology.\n\nSupported by the International Institute of Business Analysis (IIBA) Colombo Chapter as Community Partner, the session explored how Artificial Intelligence is transforming product discovery, design, and delivery within enterprise environments, while reinforcing the growing importance of product thinking as a driver of innovation, business value, and smarter decision-making.\n\nThe interactive session focused on how AI is enabling organizations to identify opportunities faster, make smarter decisions, and build products with greater clarity, speed, and impact. Discussions also explored the evolving role of product thinking in driving innovation, collaboration, and business value creation in an increasingly AI-first landscape.\n\nThe event featured a knowledge-sharing session by Tharange Abeysinghe -\u00a0 Senior Group Product Manager, alongside a panel discussion with Fawaz Haniffa \u2013 Lead Product Manager; Dilshan Weerabahu \u2013 Lead Product Manager; Atheek Razick \u2013 Senior Lead \u2013 Business Analysis, and Amila Jayawickrama \u2013 Associate Manager \u2013 Business Analysis.\n\nThe discussion was moderated by Vishmie Perera \u2013 Business Analyst, while Chamodi Wijewardana \u2013 Senior Product Manager and Malsha Mayadunne \u2013 Product Manager served as facilitators for the session."
  },
