    "chunk_size_bytes": 821,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cLet my houses stay where they are\u201d: Lalkantha tells critics to go to court\n\nColombo, June 18 (Daily Mirror) - Minister K.D. Lalkantha dismissed allegations over his properties, saying anyone with concerns should take legal action.\n\nResponding to claims made by Opposition MP Chamara Sampath Dassanayake that he owns two luxury houses in Kaduwela and Maharagama, Lalkantha said, \"Let my houses stay where they are. You don\u2019t need to be told where my houses are. If anyone has a problem, they can take legal action.\u201d\n\nHis remarks came after Dassanayake alleged at a joint opposition seminar that the Minister had built two luxury houses worth millions in Kaduwela and Maharagama.\n\nThe opposition MP also claimed that Ministers in the current government had gone back on their pledge not to use new luxury vehicles."
  },
